WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.862
For each patient, the inner query searches lab results for the same patient ID.

00:00:04.862 --> 00:00:08.017
It looks for any result outside the normal range.

00:00:08.017 --> 00:00:09.642
We do not need a count.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:12.422
We only need at least one abnormal row.

00:00:12.422 --> 00:00:15.777
That makes EXISTS a direct match for the question.

00:00:15.777 --> 00:00:19.902
Run the query and identify the patients that satisfy the condition.

00:00:19.902 --> 00:00:24.617
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:24.617 --> 00:00:28.787
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:28.787 --> 00:00:32.907
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:32.907 --> 00:00:38.287
In a real setting such as an e-commerce team finding customers who purchased a target product,

00:00:38.287 --> 00:00:43.502
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:43.502 --> 00:00:45.607
before discussing syntax.

00:00:45.607 --> 00:00:51.360
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
